        "original_id": "ce72375b-e3ee-547a-aae1-9e5a80b7b157",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Nasdaq, Inc.; Citrix Systems; International Securities Exchange Holdings\n- People: Ivers Whitman Riley\n- Places: United States; Europe; Los Angeles, California; Savannah, Georgia; Hong Kong\n- Organizations: NASDAQ stock market; Armenian Stock Exchange; Copenhagen Stock Exchange; Helsinki Stock Exchange; Iceland Stock Exchange; Riga Stock Exchange; Stockholm Stock Exchange; Tallinn Stock Exchange; NASDAQ OMX Vilnius; Hong Kong Futures Exchange\n- Topics: financial services; software; virtualization; networking; SaaS; cloud computing\n\nFacts:\n- Ivers Whitman Riley was born on September 28, 1932, in Los Angeles, California, and died on February 17, 2015, in Savannah, Georgia.\n- Hong Kong Futures Exchange had Ivers Whitman Riley as Chief Executive from 1994 to 1997 and again from 1999 to 2000.\n- International Securities Exchange had Ivers Whitman Riley as Chairman from 2002 to 2006.\n- Nasdaq, Inc. is an American multinational financial services corporation.\n- Nasdaq, Inc. owns and operates the NASDAQ stock market and is also listed on it.\n- Nasdaq, Inc. owns and operates eight European stock exchanges: Armenian Stock Exchange, Copenhagen Stock Exchange, Helsinki Stock Exchange, Iceland Stock Exchange, Riga Stock Exchange, Stockholm Stock Exchange, Tallinn Stock Exchange, and NASDAQ OMX Vilnius.\n- International Securities Exchange Holdings, Inc. is a wholly owned subsidiary of Nasdaq, Inc..\n- Citrix Systems, Inc. is an American multinational software company.\n- Citrix Systems, Inc. provides server, application, and desktop virtualization, networking, software as a service, and cloud computing technologies.",
